Step 1: Create Deployment and Check Status:
->Open Docker, go to Kubernetes, click Create, and copy/paste the commands into your command prompt (cmd):
kubectl create deployment my-app --image=nginx
kubectl get all

Step 2: Install and Verify kubectl
Install or upgrade kubectl and check its client version:
winget install -e --id Kubernetes.kubectl
kubectl version --client

Step 3: Expose the Deployment & Port Forward
Expose the deployment as a NodePort service, check the service details, and set up port forwarding:
kubectl expose deployment my-app --type=NodePort --port=80
kubectl get service my-app
kubectl port-forward service/my-app 8082:80

step4:
You can access it in your browser at http://localhost:8082
